extraction_notes: "WB20 Canada printed 157-160 (cache p158-p161, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the text layer with every dice figure on printed 159 and the top of printed 160 checked against renders. The heading Ogopogo and its lore start in the first column of printed 157; printed 158 and the first column of printed 159 describe the Ogopogo family of Lake Okanagan; the stat block headed Ogopogo Dragon, NPC & Villain, Also Known as N''ha-a-itk, runs from the first column of printed 159 to the first column of printed 160, where The Spirit Sasquatch begins. The book heads it NPC & Villain; it is imported as playable on the repo owner''s decision for this book''s creatures, and the Notes under the Experience Tables on printed 192 give it a player ladder. || XP: those Notes say the Ogopogo uses the Dragon E.P. tables; the ladder is copied from the stored xp_table of dragon-hatchling (Dragon Hatchling (Great Horned), Rifts Ultimate Edition). || STAGES: the block prints hatchling and adult figures side by side. The class''s own block is the hatchling, the stage a player character starts at, with an empty hatchling variant and an adult variant that restates attributes, M.D.C., P.P.E., Horror Factor and bonuses. || VALUES READ OFF THE RENDER (text layer in brackets): adult Spd 1D4x10+9 crawling [!D4xlO+9] or 1D6x10+80 swimming [!D6xlO+80]; adult M.D.C. 1D4x1000 +P.E. [!D4xlOOO], +2D6x100 for ancient dragons [+2D6xlOO]; hatchling M.D.C. 6D6x10 +P.E. [6D6xlO]; S.D.C.-world adult 1D4x1000 Hit Points and 4D6x100 S.D.C., hatchling 1D4x100 H.P. and 4D6x10 S.D.C. [!D4xlOO, 4D6xlO]; adult P.P.E. 2D4x100 +P.E. [2D4xlOO]; hatchling P.P.E. 2D4x10 +P.E. and +10 per level [2D4xlO]; bio-regeneration 1D4x10 M.D.C. per minute [!D4xlO]; spray 2D4x10 gallons and 1D6x10 to vampires [2D4xlO, !D6xlO]; ram 2D4x10 M.D. [2D4xlO]; adult I.S.P. 1D6x10+40 +M.E. and hatchling I.S.P. 1D4x10 +M.E. [!D6xlO+40, !D4xlO]. || ATTRIBUTES: the book lists M.A. before M.E. in both lines; hatchling I.Q. 3D6+2, M.A. 4D6, M.E. 3D6, P.S. 5D6, P.P. 3D6+3, P.E. 3D6+3, P.B. 2D6+3; adult I.Q. 2D6+12, M.A. 2D6+12, M.E. 2D6+9, P.S. 2D6+28, P.P. 2D6+10, P.E. 3D6+10, P.B. 3D6+6. Spd stored is the land crawl (hatchling 3D6, adult 1D4x10+9); the swimming speeds (6D6+30, 1D6x10+80) are natural ability text. || P.P.E.: the +10 per level is printed in the hatchling clause and stored on the hatchling only. The ancient dragon +2D6x100 M.D.C. is ability text. || BONUSES: hatchling +1 initiative, +2 strike, +1 parry and dodge, +2 pull punch, +2 roll, +3 vs Horror Factor, +1 on all other saving throws; adult +3, +4, +3, +5, +4, +7 and +3. All other saving throws is written across the fourteen d20 saves the sheet draws (the dragon hatchling precedent); coma/death is a percentage and is left out. Four physical attacks (hatchling) and seven (adult) are attacks_base; the or-by-magic counts (one, two) are ability text. || SKILLS: printed once for both stages, all at fixed figures with per_level 0. Speaks six additional languages at 98% is six picks of Language: Other; the book prints no line for speaking Dragonese itself, only literacy, so no spoken Dragonese row is stored. Demon & monster lore is Lore: Demons & Monsters; faerie lore is Lore: Faeries & Creatures of Magic; underwater navigation is Navigation: Underwater. Prowl''s +15% underwater is in its note. Six selections from six categories is a pick of six with no bonus; the book prints no skills gained by level. || MAGIC: the hatchling knows no spells (spells_starting 0, the dragon hatchling precedent); learning as a first level Wizard, the typical 3D4+2 spells by second level, and the adult and NPC spell knowledge are ability text. || PSIONICS: a variant cannot carry a psionics block, so the class stores the hatchling''s: minor, six powers from Sensitive or Healing, I.S.P. 1D4x10 +M.E., two more at levels 4, 8 and 12 (the printed level 16 is past the 15-level ladder). The adult''s (Major, 1D6x10+40 +M.E., all Sensitive plus 1D4+2 from Healing or Physical) is natural ability text and is not applied. || NOT STORED: size 60 to 100 feet, weight 4-6 tons, life span 6000 years (some to 10,000), average NPC level (adults 2D4+4, hatchlings 1D4), habitat, enemies and allies, and the six named family NPCs with their spell lists; they are GM Notes. No equipment or money is printed."
---

## Lore

For centuries people around Lake Okanagan in British Columbia told of a
serpent in the water. The valley''s native peoples knew it as N''ha-a-itk, a
lake spirit that raised storms when crossed, and gave it songs, offerings
and a wide berth. Later settlers named it Ogopogo after a children''s
story, and in time it became a well-loved local legend and mascot.

The legend was a family of dragons. The Ogopogo is a rare, wingless,
aquatic dragon that scholars of the Megaverse believed long extinct. A
mated pair fleeing persecution was stranded on Earth when Atlantis
vanished and the magic drained away, and they made the quiet lake their
home: swimming, fishing, watching humankind, raising their young and
sleeping for years at a stretch. When the ley lines burst back to life
the dragons woke with their power restored, and used it to shelter the
people around the lake. They have been its open friends, advisors and
guardians ever since, and the towns they helped rebuild are an island of
technology in the wilderness.

An Ogopogo is frightening to look at all the same: sixty to a hundred
feet of legless, finless serpent with trout-bright dark green scales, a
horse-shaped head that carries whatever horns, spines or hair it has, and
a forked tail. It swims in rolling loops with only part of its body
showing at once.

## GM Notes

The book heads the entry an NPC and villain. A player character is a
hatchling; pick that variant. The adult variant restates attributes,
M.D.C., P.P.E., Horror Factor and bonuses. Psionics stay the hatchling''s
on the sheet; give an adult its Major psionics by hand (I.S.P. 1D6x10+40
plus M.E., all Sensitive powers and 1D4+2 from Healing or Physical).

A hatchling takes two more psionic powers at levels 4, 8, 12 and 16.

Speeds: the sheet''s Spd is the crawl on land. Swimming, a hatchling moves
at 6D6+30 and an adult at 1D6x10+80.

Size 60 to 100 feet (18.3 to 30.5 m) long; weight 4-6 tons. Average life
span 6000 years, a few reaching 10,000. NPC adults average level 2D4+4
and hatchlings 1D4. Ancient dragons add 2D6x100 M.D.C.

The family of Lake Okanagan, all of whom answer to Ogopogo: Rynnex, the
father, a 17th level ancient; Marlyna, the mother, 11th level, Scrupulous;
Pryaxis, the elder brother, 1322 years old, 7th level, Principled; Crysta,
the elder sister, 1322 years old, 8th level, Scrupulous; and three
190-year-old hatchlings from a second litter: Pogolii (4th level,
Scrupulous, the studious and heroic one), Olaglyna (3rd level, Anarchist
leaning Miscreant, clever, cruel and hungry for power) and Ogo (2nd
level, Anarchist leaning Unprincipled, a cocky prankster who dreams of
being a hero). A fourth egg of that litter was stolen 190 years ago and
is presumed lost, which is one way to explain a player''s hatchling.
Rynnex''s cousin and mate were last heard of in the Atlantic before
Atlantis disappeared.

Habitat: the only known Ogopogos live in Okanagan Lake and River.
Enemies: none as such. Allies: beings of like outlook and alignment; the
family likes humans.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ogopogo');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ogopogo';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-ogopogo-class.sql');
